{"seq":3,"slug":"innovation","title":"创新管理","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/tech-strategy-radar/innovation","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"innovation-time-allocation","title":"创新时间分配","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/tech-strategy-radar/innovation/innovation-time-allocation","wordCount":1695,"readingTime":7},{"seq":2,"slug":"proof-of-concept-spikes","title":"概念验证与技术探针","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/tech-strategy-radar/innovation/proof-of-concept-spikes","wordCount":1675,"readingTime":7},{"seq":3,"slug":"emerging-tech-evaluation","title":"新兴技术评估","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/tech-strategy-radar/innovation/emerging-tech-evaluation","wordCount":2076,"readingTime":9}],"introMarkdown":"# 创新管理\n\n创新不是灵感迸发的偶然事件，而是需要结构化投入的组织能力。本章覆盖三个关键机制：如何在日常交付压力下为创新活动争取确定性的时间窗口，如何通过概念验证和技术探针在可控成本内验证假设，如何对新兴技术进行系统化评估以避免被炒作裹挟。\n\n这三篇文档与前一章的雷达方法论形成上下游关系：雷达产出的 Assess/Trial 信号正是创新管道的输入。而创新活动的产出——经过验证的技术方案——将在执行章节转化为迁移路线图和投资决策。\n"}